Git is version control software used to keep track of file and its changes.
Repository is a folder which contains files that git track.
Branch is a sub-space which contains copy of main repo.
List of commands : 
1. git init
2. git status
3. git add . / git add "file name"
4. git commit -m "message"
5. git log




